1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,410
You bought the option.

2
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:02,757
The market moved your way.

3
00:00:02,777 --> 00:00:04,143
You still lost money?

4
00:00:04,163 --> 00:00:06,084
SEBI's latest study found

5
00:00:06,104 --> 00:00:08,494
almost nine in ten F&O traders

6
00:00:08,514 --> 00:00:10,635
lost money in the year to

7
00:00:10,655 --> 00:00:11,806
March 2026.

8
00:00:11,826 --> 00:00:13,429
And about ninety-two percent

9
00:00:13,449 --> 00:00:15,002
of those losses came from

10
00:00:15,022 --> 00:00:15,759
options.

11
00:00:15,779 --> 00:00:17,101
Here's one big reason.

12
00:00:17,121 --> 00:00:18,766
An option is like an ice

13
00:00:18,786 --> 00:00:19,442
cream.

14
00:00:19,462 --> 00:00:20,933
You pay a premium for it,

15
00:00:20,953 --> 00:00:22,568
and it melts a little every

16
00:00:22,588 --> 00:00:23,493
single day.

17
00:00:23,513 --> 00:00:25,212
That melting is called time

18
00:00:25,232 --> 00:00:25,577
decay,

19
00:00:25,597 --> 00:00:26,450
or theta.

20
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:27,945
So the market has to move

21
00:00:27,965 --> 00:00:28,459
your way,

22
00:00:28,479 --> 00:00:29,020
by enough,

23
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,208
and fast enough.

24
00:00:30,228 --> 00:00:31,166
Move too slowly,

25
00:00:31,186 --> 00:00:33,283
and the melt eats your profit.

26
00:00:33,303 --> 00:00:34,634
Sellers collect that melt,

27
00:00:34,654 --> 00:00:36,076
though they take big risks

28
00:00:36,096 --> 00:00:37,097
of their own.

29
00:00:37,117 --> 00:00:38,045
Before you buy,

30
00:00:38,065 --> 00:00:38,308
ask:

31
00:00:38,328 --> 00:00:39,835
how much will this melt

32
00:00:39,855 --> 00:00:41,136
before I'm right?

33
00:00:41,156 --> 00:00:43,616
Follow The 7% Club.
